WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
Russia is

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.801
escalating attacks

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.503
with missile strikes hammering

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.838
much of that country.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.539
Several regions of the country

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.375
have been left without power today.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:08.942
But Russia's

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.043
launch of an over

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:10.944
powering spring

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:13.513
offensive seems to have not materialized,

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.148
at least not yet anyway.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.183
Joining us now is retired U.S.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.919
Army Major Mike Lyons.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.554
Major Lyons, thanks for being here.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.991
So it doesn't appear right at this moment

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.092
that Russia

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:29.129
has begun this spring offensive

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:33.466
Do you think that it is still coming

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.101
I do.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.203
What the Russians are doing right now

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:37.904
is fighting

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.339
what's called a covering force battle.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.874
And what they're doing is sending out

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.142
small units

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.377
well ahead of the main body of forces

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:44.778
they have.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.346
We know there's about 60,000

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.781
troops, three divisions

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.416
that they have in reserve there in the

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.451
in the eastern part of Ukraine.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.919
And they're sending out these small units

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:53.386
to probe

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.587
and find weaknesses

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.289
in the Ukraine military

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.023
and force

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.258
the Ukrainian military

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.060
to use resources against them.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.861
So I think this is all part

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.063
of a grander scheme.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:03.930
There's no question

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.732
Russia has the initiative

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.033
right now in that region,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.536
and this is a part of an offense

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.637
that's likely started.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.704
But what we're again

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.573
covering fierce battles with the military

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.374
refers to it

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.409
designed to show where the enemy is weak.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.778
And Ukraine's military,

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.246
you know in 20, 22

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.414
and the last year

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.450
seemed to have a lot of momentum.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.551
They were performing,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.585
I think perhaps better

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.554
than the Russians expected.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.889
But then six weeks later,

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:30.824
there are new questions

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:33.126
about whether Russia has the momentum.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.894
Now what do you think is playing off

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.130
playing out on the ground

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.232
I think what's happened

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.967
is Russia has started to learn

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.569
and that's got to be a sign

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.370
of ominous warning for Ukraine.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.772
If if Russia is learning

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.774
to do difficult tactical missions

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.775
for example,

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:51.311
river crossings we saw six months ago

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.079
the Russians had a real problem

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:53.880
crossing rivers

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.547
tactically

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.449
and survivability of their units

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.484
as they were going over.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:58.351
Now we're seeing them

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.919
do it better for Russia

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:00.920
to go on the offensive.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.921
They're going to have to perform

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.990
these more difficult tactical missions.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.391
And we're seeing indications

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.626
that they're learning from then.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.294
I think, again, that's a real warning

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.163
for the Ukrainian military.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.498
If that is the case,

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:13.733
Ukraine will have to do

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.034
the same things itself

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.302
if it wants to go the offensive

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.504
that the Dnipro River

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.371
really separates

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.340
the two forces right now.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.441
And that's a very difficult

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.208
tactical mission.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:22.609
So on

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:23.209
both sides,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.644
Russia seems to have the advantage

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.979
both in the initiative

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.581
and then in a learning process.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:29.215
Tell me a little bit

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.450
about the timing here.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.254
How critical is the timing in terms

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.488
of how much time Ukraine

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.525
has to train up on some of the new,

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.160
you know,

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.161
supplies that they're getting

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.762
from the Europeans?

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.530
And do they have

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.464
that time, given

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.031
that the Russians

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.401
seem to be preparing for an offensive

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:49.736
I think it's going to be

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.237
a very difficult mission

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.539
for them to train up.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.507
Likely they're in simulators right now.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.776
I'm sure training in Germany,

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:57.977
Grafenwöhr and other places.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.679
We brought some back to the United States

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.381
for the Patriot missiles.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.882
But until you get on the battlefield

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.983
and actually get in the weapons

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.318
systems, it's difficult.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.320
The tanks are still not there yet.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.755
We're seeing pictures of them on rail

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.890
heads, for example, in Poland.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.725
But time is not on the side of Ukraine

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:13.393
at this point.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.028
And the Russians are going to try

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.429
to to keep that initiative,

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.430
go on the offensive

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.965
and make sure that those tanks

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:19.532
don't get there.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.366
What we haven't seen,

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:20.833
though, is

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.635
the Russians try to interdict

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.736
some of those supply lines,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.871
go after rail heads,

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.905
because that's the only way

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:26.539
they're going to make it

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.340
to the battlefield

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.509
with any kind of speed and accuracy,

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.376
and that is to

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.578
get them there on rail heads.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:31.844
And so

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.146
so you haven't seen Russia do that.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:33.813
They're going to continue

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.348
to bomb infrastructure

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.916
and go after those high value

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:37.584
targets there.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.952
But but Russia right now

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.086
is doing what it does

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.221
best, and that is

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.722
bring a lot of military power

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.090
and capacity, move slowly

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.792
and destroy everything in its path.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:46.593
And we're all. Yeah.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.560
And we're also seeing them

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.328
really going

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:50.630
after civilian targets as well,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.165
which has been devastating

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.233
for the Ukrainian people.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.534
Retired U.S.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.269
Army Major Mike Lyons, thank you

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.036
for all of that.

